+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.** As it stands, `deposit()` reverts on every
+call against the real USDT at `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`. Nobody can
+put a dollar in. If that one line is fixed, the next thing you hit is that the vault
+never accrues a cent of the Aave yield it exists to collect, and permanently orphans
+both that yield and every withdrawal fee inside Aave with no function that can reach
+them. I found nine issues; two are contract-killing, three are high.
+
+Nothing under `src/` was changed. Everything below reproduces against the code exactly
+as committed at `199e2bf`.
+
+---
+
+## Contents
+
+| # | Severity | Finding |
+|---|---|---|
+| F-01 | Critical | `deposit()` reverts unconditionally against real USDT |
+| F-02 | Critical | Aave yield is never accrued, and is unrecoverable |
+| F-03 | High | `withdraw()` orphans the withdrawal fee inside Aave |
+| F-04 | High | `depositFeeBps` is unbounded and takes effect instantly |
+| F-05 | High | `pause()` also blocks `withdraw()` |
+| F-06 | Medium | Neither fee is collectible by anyone |
+| F-07 | Medium | Dust shares cannot be redeemed |
+| F-08 | Medium | No constructor validation; single-step ownership |
+| F-09 | Medium | No handling of USDT's transfer-fee switch |
+| F-10 | Info | Dead `aUsdt`, ignored return values, inconsistent events |
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce everything
+
+New files, all under `test/`:
+
+```
+test/AccountingBugs.t.sol           share/asset accounting          (offline)
+test/OwnerRisk.t.sol                what the owner key can do       (offline)
+test/UsdtQuirks.t.sol               USDT semantics, offline repro   (offline)
+test/VaultInvariants.t.sol          stateful invariants             (offline)
+test/fork/RealUsdt.t.sol            real USDT + real Aave V3        (needs RPC)
+test/fork/AaveYieldAccrual.t.sol    real Aave V3                    (needs RPC)
+test/harness/TetherLikeUsdt.sol     TetherToken-faithful stand-in
+test/harness/VaultHandler.sol       invariant handler
+```
+
+The fork tests pin mainnet **block 25,000,000** and default to the public archive
+endpoint `https://eth.drpc.org`. Override with `MAINNET_RPC_URL` if you have your own.
+
+These are written as tests that assert what a safe vault *should* do, so a `[FAIL]`
+line is the finding. To run the team's original suite on its own:
+
+```
+forge test --no-match-path 'test/{fork/*,AccountingBugs.t.sol,OwnerRisk.t.sol,UsdtQuirks.t.sol,VaultInvariants.t.sol}'
+```
