+## F-01 — Critical — `deposit()` reverts unconditionally against real USDT
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:93`
+
+```solidity
+usdt.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);   // <-- raw IERC20.approve
+```
+
+`safeTransferFrom` goes through `SafeERC20` and is fine. The very next line does not:
+it calls `IERC20.approve` directly. `IERC20.approve` is declared `returns (bool)`, so
+solc emits a returndata check and ABI-decodes 32 bytes. The deployed `TetherToken`
+declares `function approve(address, uint) public` with **no return value**, so it
+returns zero bytes and the decode reverts. Every deposit, every size, every time.
+
+There is a second, independent reason the same line is unsafe: `TetherToken.approve`
+contains `require(!((_value != 0) && (allowed[msg.sender][_spender] != 0)))`, so a
+non-zero → non-zero allowance change reverts. `deposit()` calls `approve(amount)`
+unconditionally, so any residual allowance to the Aave pool bricks it permanently.
+
