+The same two failures reproduce offline against a TetherToken-faithful stand-in, if
+you would rather not depend on an RPC (`test_DepositWorksAgainstUsdtSemantics` and
+`test_UsdtAllowsOverwritingANonZeroAllowance` in the F-09 transcript below).
+
+Note the user's USDT is taken *before* the revert reverts it — the transaction as a
+whole rolls back, so no funds are lost. The vault is simply unusable.
+
+**Fix.** Use `SafeERC20` for the approval too. `usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount)`
+handles both problems: it tolerates empty returndata, and on failure it retries after
+zeroing the allowance. Alternatively approve `type(uint256).max` once in the
+constructor via `forceApprove` and drop the per-deposit approval entirely.
