+## F-02 — Critical — Aave yield is never accrued, and is unrecoverable
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:139-141`
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return totalAssetsStored;
+}
+```
+
+`totalAssetsStored` is a plain counter, written only by `deposit()` and `withdraw()`.
+The vault's actual position is its aUSDT balance, which grows every block. Nothing in
+the contract ever reads it — `aUsdt` is assigned in the constructor and never used
+again:
+
+```
+$ grep -n "aUsdt" src/UsdtYieldVault.sol
+41:    IERC20 public immutable aUsdt;
+68:    /// @param _aUsdt The Aave aUSDT receipt token.
+72:    constructor(address _usdt, address _aUsdt, address _aavePool, uint256 _depositFeeBps, address initialOwner)
+76:        aUsdt = IERC20(_aUsdt);
+```
+
+So `sharePrice()` never moves, `balanceOfUnderlying()` never grows, and a depositor
+redeems principal minus the exit fee no matter how long they stayed. The yield is not
+merely undistributed — the ABI contains no function that can move it:
+
+```
+$ forge inspect src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:UsdtYieldVault methods
