+## F-03 — High — `withdraw()` orphans the withdrawal fee inside Aave
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:107-118`
+
+```solidity
+uint256 grossAssets = convertToAssets(shares);
+uint256 fee = (grossAssets * WITHDRAW_FEE_BPS) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;
+netAssets = grossAssets - fee;
+...
+totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets;          // books lose the whole gross
+aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), netAssets, msg.sender);   // only net leaves Aave
+```
+
+The fee is subtracted from the vault's books but never withdrawn from Aave and never
+credited to anyone. README says the opposite:
+
+> Both fees stay supplied in Aave and accrue to the remaining shareholders — they are
+> not swept to the owner.
+
+The first half is true; the second is not. Because `convertToAssets` divides by
+`totalAssetsStored`, and `totalAssetsStored` was debited by the full gross, the
+remaining shareholders' claim is completely unchanged. 30 bps of every exit is
+destroyed.
+
+**Evidence** — offline, using the project's own mocks (deposit fee 0 to isolate):
+
